WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.360
"How to Boost Fat Burning by 25%"

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:09.200
We now know why fiber-rich foods

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:11.440
can have such a powerful effect
on our weight.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.760
The evidence for the role
of fiber in weight control

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:16.480
started with so-called
ecological studies.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:19.120
These involve comparing
population averages,

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:20.240
and researchers noted

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:22.720
that populations
with extraordinary fiber intakes

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:25.680
tend to have
negligible obesity rates.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:28.240
For example, the average
Pima Indian in Mexico

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:30.000
eating their traditional
high-fiber diet

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.680
centered around
the "three sisters"

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:33.360
(corn, beans, and squash)

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:34.960
is normal weight,

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:39.280
but the average Pima on U.S.
reservations has obesity.

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:41.520
The problem with dealing
with population averages

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:42.320
is that we don’t know

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:44.640
if the individuals eating
the higher-fiber diets

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:48.560
are themselves necessarily
the ones protected from obesity.

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:50.080
What do we see
in cohort studies,

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:53.280
where individuals and their
diets are followed over time?

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:55.280
A cohort study
of overweight youth found

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:56.560
that the amount of fiber found

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:59.280
in a single half cup
daily serving of beans,

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:00.960
about 6 grams,

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.560
over about a two-year period,

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:05.520
was associated
with a profound 25% difference

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:08.240
in abdominal obesity.

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:09.920
In about the same timeframe,

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:11.120
in middle-aged women,

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:13.280
each 2-gram increase
in daily fiber

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:15.200
was associated
with a weight decrease

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:18.160
of about a pound (0.45 kg).

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:20.240
The postpartum period
seems to be a critical time

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:21.920
for women to be
at risk of retaining

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:24.400
the weight put on
during pregnancy.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:26.000
A study of hundreds of new moms

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:27.760
followed for the first
five months

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:29.680
found that inadequate
fiber intake

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:33.040
appeared to increase
obesity risk by 24%.

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:34.960
And it’s not just women.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:37.360
A cohort that included
tens of thousands of men

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:38.640
followed for years

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:40.880
concluded that an increase
in fiber consumption

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:42.640
of just 10 grams a day

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:46.240
may prevent about 10% of weight
gain within the population.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:50.640
Overall, the evidence from these
kinds of observational studies

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:51.680
is strong that

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:53.600
"Increasing consumption
of dietary fiber

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:56.640
with fruits, vegetables,
whole grains, and legumes

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:58.080
across the life cycle

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:02.880
is a critical step in stemming
the epidemic of obesity."

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:05.440
These studies can control
for nondietary influences

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:07.040
such as physical activity

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:10.560
by equipping people with gadgets
to measure their movement,

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:13.760
but there may be uncontrolled
confounding dietary factors.

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:16.560
Think about the list
of high-fiber foods--

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:19.680
fruits, vegetables,
whole grains, and beans.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:21.120
Maybe fiber intake is just

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:24.000
a marker for the intake
of healthy foods,

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.640
and there are dozens of reasons
why eating whole plant foods

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:30.240
could lead to weight loss that
have nothing to do with fiber.

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:32.240
To know if there’s
a cause-and-effect relationship

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:34.640
between fiber and weight loss,

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:38.240
you need to put it to the test
in interventional trials.

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:41.200
That’s where colonic infusions
can come in handy.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:42.560
In a randomized, double-blind,

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:44.400
placebo-controlled
crossover study,

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:47.360
researchers showed that people’s
metabolism can be boosted

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:50.000
within 30 minutes of
an infusion into their rectums

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.520
of short-chain fatty acids,

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:55.680
the molecules our gut bacteria
make when we feed them fiber.

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:58.480
The study used the amounts
we’d expect to create ourselves

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:01.200
just from eating
a high-fiber diet.

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:03.440
Not only did the study
participants get an increase

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:05.200
in their resting metabolic rate

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:08.080
(the amount of calories burned
just by existing),

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:11.440
but specifically, their fat
oxidation shot up as well,

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:13.120
increasing the amount
of fat they were burning

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:15.840
by more than 25%.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:16.880
This translates to about

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:19.600
an extra third of a pat
of butter’s worth of fat

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:23.360
burned off their body within
two hours of the infusion.

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:25.280
Colonic catheters aside,

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:27.520
we can get short-chain
fatty acids directly

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:28.800
and get the same little bump

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:32.320
in resting metabolic rate
and whole-body fat breakdown

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:35.280
in addition
to a decrease in appetite.

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:37.520
So again, fiber may work
on both sides

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:39.920
of the energy balance equation.

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:41.520
But does that decreased appetite

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:44.000
actually translate
into eating less?

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:46.559
We’ll find out next.

